#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Measure and ratchet recurring Flutter performance anti-patterns across the workspace.

Mirrors the conventions of tool/ds-audit and tool/structure-audit:
  tool/perf-audit                     summary + baseline comparison (exit 0)
  tool/perf-audit --check             exit 1 if any file/rule count grew or an allow is malformed
  tool/perf-audit --update-baseline   lower tool/perf-audit-baseline.json (integration branch only)
  tool/perf-audit --json              print the aggregated report as JSON
  tool/perf-audit --git-ref REF       scan files at a git ref without touching the working tree

Workflow: a feature branch only has to keep every file/rule count at or below
tool/perf-audit-baseline.json and never edits the baseline file (parallel branches
that lower the same file would conflict on it). After merges, the integration owner
runs `tool/perf-audit --update-baseline` and commits the lowered baseline separately.

Rules and before/after fixes: docs/perf-tuning-guide.md.
Escape hatch for reviewed exceptions (requires a non-empty reason):
  // perf-allow: <reason>    on the offending line or the line directly above.
"""
